// An #analog reading is UNSIGNED by default -- unlike a #variable. A converter
// delivers counts, 0..2^res-1; `integer` is the opt-in for a reading about a
// rest point, an accelerometer's 0 = level.
//
// The value slot is `unsigned val:16` and cannot hold a negative, so a signed
// analog stores the low 16 bits and gets them sign-extended on the way out.
//
// The declaration's vt used to be dropped entirely on this path: `signed`
// parsed and meant nothing at all.

#analog Sg:16 integer inout 0:2
#analog Un:16 inout 0:3            // unsigned by default

#variable a = 0
#variable b = 0

// 0xF000 has bit 15 set. Signed it is -4096; unsigned it is 61440.
Sg = 0xF000 ? 1
Un = 0xF000 ? 1

a = Sg ? 1
b = Un ? 1
